Simple Explanation
CREATE TABLE staging.orders (

Creates a new table named orders inside the staging schema.

order_id INT PRIMARY KEY,

Stores the unique ID of each order.

PRIMARY KEY means duplicate order_ids are not allowed inside the valid staging table.

customer_id INT,

Identifies which customer placed the order.

order_date DATE,

Stores the business date when the order happened.

status VARCHAR(20),

Stores statuses such as:

completed
cancelled
pending
total_amount NUMERIC(12,2),

Stores the total monetary value of the order.

created_at TIMESTAMPTZ,

Stores when the source system created the record.

source_file VARCHAR(255),

Keeps the filename where the record came from.

This helps with data lineage.

ingested_at TIMESTAMPTZ,

Stores when our pipeline loaded the record.

batch_id INT

Identifies which ingestion batch processed the record.

Rejected Orders Table
CREATE TABLE staging.orders_rejected (
    order_id INT,
    customer_id INT,
    order_date DATE,
    status VARCHAR(20),
    total_amount NUMERIC(12,2),
