10. Referential Integrity Check

We checked whether every order item belongs to a valid order.

SELECT
    oi.order_item_id,
    oi.order_id
FROM raw.order_items oi
LEFT JOIN staging.orders o
    ON oi.order_id = o.order_id
WHERE o.order_id IS NULL;
Explanation
FROM raw.order_items oi

Starts with order items.

oi is just an alias.

LEFT JOIN staging.orders o

Tries to find the corresponding valid order.

ON oi.order_id = o.order_id

Matches them using order_id.

WHERE o.order_id IS NULL

Returns items where no valid parent order exists.

These are called:

Orphan records

